# Normalise line endings so a clone on any platform produces the same bytes.
# This matters here for two concrete reasons:
#   1. noct-demo-wasm/build.sh, quickstart.sh and demo-transaction.sh are executed
#      by bash on Linux/CI. A CRLF checkout yields "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r" and dies
#      with a bad-interpreter error, even though the same tree works on Windows.
#   2. cmd/schedprobe/expected.txt is the golden output for the WASI runtime gate.
#      tools/build-guest.ps1 normalises CRLF before diffing, so it tolerates either
#      form -- but pinning LF removes the ambiguity rather than relying on that.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf

# Never normalise binaries. Rewriting a byte of noct-demo.wasm would invalidate the
# sha256 recorded in artifacts/BUILD-EVIDENCE.md and in 31-DEPLOYMENT-ARCHITECTURE.md.
*.wasm binary
*.exe binary
*.zip binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
